{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016LZnJttmUPnhkDMtxaMD7Q","type":"tool_result","content":"560\t  reported the crash as a warning, which reads as green. It\n561\t  now exits 2 with a named error in each of those cases. It checks the\n562\t  containers of `hooks`, not every field (Known-open below).\n563\t\n564\t### Fixed — two parallel audit writers could leave a chain break nobody caused (v1.4.0-rc.1 condition 67)\n565\t\n566\t- `append_entry` in `.claude/hooks/audit_log.py` writes the `agent_spawn`\n567\t  events. It used to read the previous link (`audit-log.last-hmac`) and\n568\t  compute the line's HMAC before taking the log lock. If another writer\n569\t  appended in between (another `agent_spawn`, or an `audit_emit` event), the\n570\t  line was chained to a stale link, and `verify_chain()` reported\n571\t  `hmac_mismatch` with no tampering.\n572\t- It now does four things under one log lock: reads the link, computes the\n573\t  HMAC, appends the line and updates the sidecar. It is the same lock under\n574\t  which `audit_emit` and the spool drain already read the link and append.\n575\t- **This release retires signed condition 67 of v1.4.0-rc.1.** That\n576\t  condition is the parallel-writer break described in the `[1.4.0]` entry.\n577\t  Breaks the race already wrote stay in your logs (Known-open below).\n578\t- When this writer rotates the log, line 1 of the new log is the\n579\t  `chain_reset_marker` (ADR-055-AMEND-2), and the `agent_spawn` line chains\n580\t  to it.\n581\t- If that marker is not on disk, the line is written without an HMAC\n582\t  (`hmac_error=chain_reset_marker_missing`). It stays outside the chain, and\n583\t  `check-audit-hmac-null.py` shows it.\n584\t- A lock timeout still drops the line and leaves a breadcrumb, without\n585\t  blocking the session.\n586\t- Both shipped settings templates register `audit_log.py`, and `upgrade.sh`\n587\t  delivers the cured file.\n588\t\n589\t### Changed — a fresh `--ceremony user` install writes `permissions.defaultMode: \"manual\"` (PLAN-194 W5b)\n590\t\n591\t- `install.sh` writes `\"manual\"` together with the deny baseline when the\n592\t  `.claude/settings.json` produced by that same run has no\n593\t  `permissions.defaultMode`. It does so on both of its routes, `jq` and\n594\t  `python3`. When no settings source sets `defaultMode`, Claude Code"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87055104-8462-4c4d-860e-1d287a85b12f","uuid":"e5ebb544-e365-4ec9-b247-64d9c4034e56","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:31:12.056Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  reported the crash as a warning, which reads as green. It\n  now exits 2 with a named error in each of those cases. It checks the\n  containers of `hooks`, not every field (Known-open below).\n\n### Fixed — two parallel audit writers could leave a chain break nobody caused (v1.4.0-rc.1 condition 67)\n\n- `append_entry` in `.claude/hooks/audit_log.py` writes the `agent_spawn`\n  events. It used to read the previous link (`audit-log.last-hmac`) and\n  compute the line's HMAC before taking the log lock. If another writer\n  appended in between (another `agent_spawn`, or an `audit_emit` event), the\n  line was chained to a stale link, and `verify_chain()` reported\n  `hmac_mismatch` with no tampering.\n- It now does four things under one log lock: reads the link, computes the\n  HMAC, appends the line and updates the sidecar. It is the same lock under\n  which `audit_emit` and the spool drain already read the link and append.\n- **This release retires signed condition 67 of v1.4.0-rc.1.** That\n  condition is the parallel-writer break described in the `[1.4.0]` entry.\n  Breaks the race already wrote stay in your logs (Known-open below).\n- When this writer rotates the log, line 1 of the new log is the\n  `chain_reset_marker` (ADR-055-AMEND-2), and the `agent_spawn` line chains\n  to it.\n- If that marker is not on disk, the line is written without an HMAC\n  (`hmac_error=chain_reset_marker_missing`). It stays outside the chain, and\n  `check-audit-hmac-null.py` shows it.\n- A lock timeout still drops the line and leaves a breadcrumb, without\n  blocking the session.\n- Both shipped settings templates register `audit_log.py`, and `upgrade.sh`\n  delivers the cured file.\n\n### Changed — a fresh `--ceremony user` install writes `permissions.defaultMode: \"manual\"` (PLAN-194 W5b)\n\n- `install.sh` writes `\"manual\"` together with the deny baseline when the\n  `.claude/settings.json` produced by that same run has no\n  `permissions.defaultMode`. It does so on both of its routes, `jq` and\n  `python3`. When no settings source sets `defaultMode`, Claude Code","numLines":35,"startLine":560,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016LZnJttmUPnhkDMtxaMD7Q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
