s covered by the restored kernel rows, so conditions 5 and 7 hold; with no P0 or undeclared P1 found, only P2 follow-ups remain on top of the release's declared conditions.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"PAYLOAD 3/32 — what it contains: the new files _lib/_audit_emit_parts/{orchestration,pair_rail,planning,rate_limits,replay,resource_events,routing,security,streaming,tokens_boot,workflow,writer}.py, plus _lib/_audit_log_parts/__init__.py, adapters_runtime.py and the first part of entries_usage.py. This is PLAN-197 / ADR-202 code moved out of the old monolithic _lib/audit_emit.py and audit_log.py.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED (against the candidate tree)\n1. How the moved code is loaded.\n   - audit_emit.py:413-452 imports each part. _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48 then deep-copies the values and rebuilds each function with the facade's globals (`FunctionType(code, facade_globals, ...)`). Global lookups, `global` writes (writer.py `_FALLBACK_NOTIFIED`), `globals()` (orchestration.py `_try_rate_admit`) and test patch points therefore all go through the facade, as they did in the monolith.\n   - The lookups the payload's functions make at call time all resolve to a name exported by an installed part (operations, boot_schemas, governance, lifecycle_schemas, harness_schemas, adapters) or defined in the facade: `_PLAN088_RATE_LOCK` and `_PLAN090_BUCKET_LOCK` (audit_emit.py:483-484), `emit_generic`, `_KNOWN_ACTIONS`, `EVENT_SCHEMA_V2`.\n   - Code that runs when a part is imported only uses names that part defines or imports itself: `time` in rate_limits and streaming; with `from __future__ import annotations`, annotations are never evaluated.\n   - I found no duplicate export among the names I sampled across parts, so no silent override.\n   - The `audit_hmac._ensure_canonical_lib_modules` pollution check (audit_hmac.py:760-805) reads only the module `__file__`, so the parts cannot trigger a false `hmac:null`.\n2. audit_log.py:311-327 runs paths_skills, entries_usage, rotation_storage and adapters_runtime with `exec` in its own namespace.\n   - adapters_runtime runs last, and its `if __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())` (adapters_runtime.py:258) fires only after every declaration exists.\n   - `main()`, `_codex_audit_main` and `_grok_audit_main` are identical to the older staged monolith (.claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1/tree/.claude/hooks/audit_log.py:1360-1616), and so is `build_entry` (:579-703).\n3. Model and effort: `_ADR_052_ROLE_TO_MODEL` (entries_usage.py:347-379) matches the staged table except for the v1.4.2 (PLAN-193) \"general-purpose\" -> claude-opus-5-5 row. Nothing in this delta changes it, and it only feeds the audit record's policy fallback, never routing.\n4. Fail direction.\n   - The audit writers remain fail-open.\n   - A crash at import (for example a missing part) produces no decision. `_python-hook.sh:416` then hands the exit code to the hook itself (`exec`), and on the grok blocking path `_python-hook.sh:548` returns the hook's own exit code. Only exit 2 blocks, so the session is not blocked.\n5. Condition 5: check_arbitration_kernel.py:312-313 lists `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*` and `_audit_log_parts/**/*`, and `_fnmatch_segments` (:365-390) treats `**` as zero or more segments, so every file in this payload is a kernel path. TRUE.\n6. Condition 7: both entry points keep their paths, and the logic now lives in kernel-listed modules. TRUE.\n7. Delivery:\n   - scripts/install.sh:1520-1549 copies every top-level `_lib` entry.\n   - scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-105 does not exclude `_audit_*_parts`.\n8. Python and dependencies: standard library only (copy, importlib, types, typing, time, re). I found no syntax or API newer than Python 3.9.\n9. Honesty: CHANGELOG [1.4.4] says \"_lib/audit_emit.py goes from 14,522 lines to 496\", and the facade is 496 lines. It also claims no differential replay, which is accurate.\n\nP0: none.\nP1: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS (the code appears carried over from the monolith; I could not read the base text of audit_emit.py, so I do not count these as regressions from this delta)\n\nP2-1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/writer.py:758-761 (with :603-604 and filelock.py:144)\n- Failure scenario: the F-CHAOS-1 fallback references `line` before it is assigned.\n  - If the primary audit directory is unwritable and audit-log.lock does not exist yet, `FileLock.__enter__` raises OSError (EACCES) at :604. `os.open(O_CREAT)` in filelock.py:144 is the call that fails, before `line` is built at :687.\n  - The except branch at :758 prints the \"::warning:: ... falling back to <fallback>\" banner and then calls `_write_fallback(line)`. That raises UnboundLocalError, which the outer `except` swallows.\n  - The event is lost while stderr says it was diverted.\n- Why tests miss it: test_audit_emit.py:1183-1211 injects the PermissionError at `Path.open` on the log, after `line` exists.\n- Minimal fix: serialize the fallback line from `event` inside the except branch, as the FileLockTimeout branch already does at :751. Add a test that makes the lock path uncreatable.\n\nP2-2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/writer.py:38-51, :76, :87\n- Failure scenario: the fallback path `/tmp/ceo-audit-fallback-<user>.log` is predictable.\n  - It is opened with `Path.open(\"a\")`, then `os.chmod`-ed, and both calls follow symlinks.\n  - On a shared host without protected_symlinks (stock macOS /private/tmp), another local user can plant that name as a symlink. When the victim's primary write fails or the lock times out, audit JSON is appended to a file the victim owns, and that file is chmod-ed to 0600.\n- Minimal fix: `os.open(path, O_WRONLY|O_APPEND|O_CREAT|O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)` plus `fchmod` on the descriptor, or a per-user 0700 directory with the same trust gate `_python-hook.sh:173-198` uses.\n\nP2-3 — .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:382-383, :455-461 and _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:4-6\n- The package docstring promises that `inspect.isfunction` stays intact \"with no proxy per event\". `iter_events` is now a plain wrapper around the rebound generator, kept so the AST check in check-audit-read-api-stable.py stays green.\n- Consequence: `inspect.isgeneratorfunction(audit_emit.iter_events)` is now False.\n- Fix: state the exception in the docstring, or bind the generator directly and adapt the AST check.\n\nP2-4 — .claude/hooks/audit_log.py:317-324\n- The parts loader has no guard. A missing or unreadable `_lib/_audit_log_parts/*.py` (partial or hand-edited upgrade) raises FileNotFoundError at import.\n  - The hook exits 1 with a traceback and leaves no breadcrumb, which contradicts the module docstring's \"Safety properties 1\" (exit 0 plus a breadcrumb).\n  - It is still fail-open through `_python-hook.sh`, and it is the same class as the unguarded `_lib` imports at :174-179.\n- Related: the part files sit in a package (`__init__.py`), yet they cannot be imported on their own (entries_usage.py:149 uses `re` without importing it). Nothing shipped imports them.\n- Fix: guard the loader in the `__main__` path (breadcrumb, then exit 0).\n\nP2-5 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py, actions_core.py, actions_extended.py (not in this payload's diff)\n- These files ship but are absent from the facade's install list (audit_emit.py:415-451), and nothing imports them. That leaves a second copy of `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` beside the facade literal (audit_emit.py:45-377).\n- The actions I sampled match today, so the risk is future drift.\n- Fix: remove them, or install `actions` and drop the literal (adjusting the scripts that read the literal).\n\nP2-6 — stale line references in moved docstrings and comments\n- pair_rail.py:85 and routing.py:420 (\"audit_emit.py:386-396\").\n- orchestration.py:217 (\"line ~3484\").\n- audit_hmac.py:772 still says \"chokepoints 1/3 in audit_emit.py\"; they now live in writer.py.\n- Cosmetic.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS vs THIS PAYLOAD: conditions 5, 7, 13 and 14 hold for these files. Nothing here contradicts conditions 1-4, 6 or 8-12.","decision":"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS","sentence":"The moved audit-writer code in this payload is identical where it could be compared with an older copy, resolves every name through the facade, stays fail-open and standard-library-only on Python 3.9, and every file is covered by the restored kernel rows, so conditions 5 and 7 hold; with no P0 or undeclared P1 found, only P2 follow-ups remain on top of the release's declared conditions."},"ttft_ms":5336,"type":"result","duration_ms":563150,"uuid":"2abc5e78-7173-4dac-ae21-faf3e8f07353","ttft_stream_ms":4196,"time_to_request_ms":199,"first_content_frame_ms":4196,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":104,"outputTokens":47176,"cacheReadInputTokens":9733706,"cacheCreationInputTokens":242753,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.832701199999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":31301,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":242753,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-20T15:54:23.997Z"}
